From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:56:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Check the CSP of a media request before the media
 cache serves it

The media cache shares a resource among the media elements of a content
process that request it with the same URL, CORS mode and document origin,
and serves it without a fetch once it holds it. Net checks a request
against the Content Security Policy of its client only when it fetches
it, so a document whose policy blocks the media resource could play it
from the cache after a document of the same origin with another policy
had loaded it.

Run "should request be blocked by Content Security Policy?" on the request
that the media element would make before it opens a reader, with the
policy list of the document, and report the violations. A blocked request
runs the media data processing steps for media data that cannot be
fetched at all, in a media element task, as a blocked fetch does.

The fetcher no longer queues the failure steps itself when its first
fetch fails: the cache reports such a failure to every reader as a
network error, which runs the same steps whether the fetch was blocked or
failed, and the only block that differs between documents sharing a
resource, CSP, is now checked before the reader opens.

Fork note: meant for upstream. Drop once upstream has it.

Testing: content-security-policy/media-src covers blocked and allowed
media requests, also from blob and data URLs.

Validation: the 10 tests of content-security-policy/media-src give the
expected results. `./mach test-wpt --release --timeout-multiplier 2` on Linux with
GStreamer of html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements and
the-video-element, html/canvas/element/manual/drawing-images-to-the-canvas
and imagebitmap, fetch/range, content-security-policy/media-src,
html/browsers/browsing-the-web/read-media and
mozilla/media-autoplay-seek-after-ended.html with the series, 507 tests:
the unexpected results also occur with the phase 1 build of ohos-main
(load-removes-queued-error-event hangs, media_fragment_seek fails,
track-remove-by-setting-innerHTML timed out 1 of 6 isolated runs here
and 2 of 6 there, autoplay-default-permissions-policy passes where a
timeout is expected); loop-from-ended failed 1 of 26 isolated runs here
and 1 of 26 there. `./mach check` and `./mach check --ohos` pass.

AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; implemented and tested by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
